    "engine": "jupyter",
    "markdown": "---\ngd-head-tags:\n  - >-\n    `<script type=\"application/ld+json\">[{\"@context\": \"https://schema.org\",\n    \"@type\": \"SoftwareSourceCode\", \"name\": \"EdgeCase\", \"description\":\n    \"High-performance graph analysis library\", \"codeRepository\":\n    \"https://github.com/rich-iannone/edgecase\", \"license\":\n    \"https://opensource.org/licenses/MIT\", \"url\":\n    \"https://rich-iannone.github.io/edgecase\", \"documentation\":\n    \"https://rich-iannone.github.io/edgecase\", \"programmingLanguage\": {\"@type\":\n    \"ComputerLanguage\", \"name\": \"Python\"}}, {\"@context\": \"https://schema.org\",\n    \"@type\": \"WebPage\", \"name\": \"Graph.find_negative_cycle - EdgeCase\",\n    \"isPartOf\": {\"@type\": \"WebSite\", \"name\": \"EdgeCase\"}, \"url\":\n    \"https://rich-iannone.github.io/edgecase/reference/Graph.find_negative_cycle.html\"}]</script>`{=html}\nopen-graph:\n  title: >-\n    [Graph.find_negative_cycle()]{.doc-object-name .doc-function .doc-label\n    .doc-label-method} | EdgeCase\n  description: >-\n    Find a cycle of negative total weight reachable from a source node.\ntwitter-card:\n  title: >-\n    [Graph.find_negative_cycle()]{.doc-object-name .doc-function .doc-label\n    .doc-label-method} | EdgeCase\n  description: >-\n    Find a cycle of negative total weight reachable from a source node.\ntitle: >-\n  [Graph.find_negative_cycle()]{.doc-object-name .doc-function .doc-label\n  .doc-label-method}\nbody-classes: doc-api-page doc-py-api-page\nshift-heading-level-by: 0\nbread-crumbs: false\ntoc-depth: 3\ndescription-meta: >-\n  Find a cycle of negative total weight reachable from a source node.\npage-navigation: false\nhtml-table-processing: none\n---\n\n::: {.doc-subject}\n\nFind a cycle of negative total weight reachable from a source node.\n:::\n\n::: {.doc-usage-source}\nUsage\n\n[Source](https://github.com/rich-iannone/edgecase/blob/main/python/edgecase/graph.py#L59505-L59607){target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"}\n:::\n\n::: {.doc-signature .doc-function}\n```pythonsignature\nGraph.find_negative_cycle(\n    source,\n    weighted=None,\n)\n```\n:::\n\n::: {.doc-text}\n\n![Find negative cycle](../assets/graphs/find-negative-cycle.light.svg){.lightbox fig-alt=\"Three currencies linked by exchange edges weighted with negative log-rates, searched from USD (outlined). Going around USD to EUR to GBP and back to USD (accent arrows) costs −0.10 − 0.15 + 0.20 = −0.05, a negative cycle: an arbitrage loop. The card returns the cycle with its first node repeated at the end, USD, EUR, GBP, USD.\" width=\"100%\"}\n\nReturns one negative cycle that can be reached from `source`, as the list of nodes\naround it (the first node repeated at the end). Use it to locate the arbitrage loop or\nthe modelling error behind a failed shortest-path computation (see\n`negative_edge_cycle()`).\n:::\n\n## Parameters {.doc-parameters}\n\n::: {.doc-definition-items}\n<code>[source]{.doc-parameter-name}[:]{.doc-parameter-annotation-sep} [Union[int, str]]{.doc-parameter-annotation}</code>\n\n:   The node to search from, as an ID or label.\n\n<code>[weighted]{.doc-parameter-name}[:]{.doc-parameter-annotation-sep} [bool | None]{.doc-parameter-annotation} [=]{.doc-parameter-default-sep .op} [None]{.doc-parameter-default}</code>\n\n:   Whether to use edge weights. If `None` (default), follows the graph's `weighted`\n    flag.\n:::\n\n## Returns {.doc-returns}\n\n::: {.doc-definition-items}\n<code> [list[int]]{.doc-parameter-annotation}</code>\n\n:   The node IDs around the cycle, with the first node repeated at the end.\n:::\n\n## Raises {.doc-raises}\n\n::: {.doc-definition-items}\n<code> [ValueError]{.doc-parameter-annotation}</code>\n\n:   If `source` does not exist or no negative cycle is reachable from it.\n:::\n\n## Technical Notes {.doc-technical-notes}\n\nBellman-Ford from `source`, keeping predecessors. A node still improving in round $V$ is\nreachable from a negative cycle; following predecessors $V$ times lands on the cycle,\nwhich is then read off by following predecessors until it closes. It runs in $O(VE)$\ntime. NetworkX's `find_negative_cycle` can fail with \"Negative cycle is detected but not\nfound\" on some graphs where this method succeeds.\n\n## See Also {.doc-see-also}\n\n[](`~negative_edge_cycle`) \n\n:   Check whether any negative cycle exists.\n\n[](`~bellman_ford_shortest_path`) \n\n:   Shortest paths with negative weights, if no cycle is negative.\n\n## Examples {.doc-examples}\n\nThree currencies whose exchange rates, as negative log-rates, make a loop of negative total\nweight, `-0.10 - 0.15 + 0.20 = -0.05`:\n\n::: {#3de5c1c0 .cell execution_count=1}\n``` {.python .cell-code}\nimport edgecase as ec\n\nfx = ec.Graph.from_edges(\n    [(\"USD\", \"EUR\", -0.10), (\"EUR\", \"GBP\", -0.15), (\"GBP\", \"USD\", 0.20)],\n    directed=True,\n)\n\n[fx.get_label_from_id(n) for n in fx.find_negative_cycle(\"USD\")]\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display execution_count=1}\n```\n['USD', 'EUR', 'GBP', 'USD']\n```\n:::\n:::\n\n\n### Finding an arbitrage\n\n`currency()` holds the exchange rates quoted between six currencies, each edge weighted by\nthe negative log of its rate, and its stale euro–pound quotes make an arbitrage loop.\nSearching from the Canadian dollar finds it, since every currency can reach it:\n\n::: {#ab122a61 .cell execution_count=2}\n``` {.python .cell-code}\nfx = ec.currency()\nloop = fx.find_negative_cycle(\"CAD\")\n\n[fx.get_label_from_id(n) for n in loop]\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display execution_count=2}\n```\n['GBP', 'USD', 'EUR', 'GBP']\n```\n:::\n:::\n\n\nMultiplying the rates around the loop gives the gain on each pound, euro or dollar that\ngoes around it, about 0.1%:\n\n::: {#dc288ec3 .cell execution_count=3}\n``` {.python .cell-code}\nimport math\n\nedges = fx.get_edge_df()\npairs = list(zip(edges[\"source\"], edges[\"target\"]))\nrate = dict(zip(pairs, edges[\"rate\"]))\n\nsteps = list(zip(loop, loop[1:]))\nround(math.prod(rate[step] for step in steps), 5)\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display execution_count=3}\n```\n1.00099\n```\n:::\n:::\n\n\n::: {#cf4b1ec4 .cell execution_count=4}\n``` {.python .cell-code}\nfx.plot(highlight=steps, label_by=\"label\", curved_edges=True, seed=4)\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display execution_count=4}\n```{=html}\n<div class=\"ec-theme\" style=\"display:contents\"><style class=\"ec-theme-vars\">:where(.ec-theme){--ect-3239c383:#fafafa;--ect-e5dfd507:#94a3b8;--ect-8a2de1d4:#374151;--ect-57425a7e:rgba(15,23,42,0.88);--ect-21ade003:#f1f5f9;--ect-61169ea5:#c2410c;--ect-63cc1385:#d4d4d8;--ect-879b7ebc:#949497;--ect-b9f8de6d:#872d08;--ect-f59ba8df:#a1a1aa}@media (prefers-color-scheme: dark){.ec-theme{--ect-3239c383:#0d1117;--ect-e5dfd507:#4b5563;--ect-8a2de1d4:#d1d5db;--ect-57425a7e:rgba(241,245,249,0.92);--ect-21ade003:#0f172a;--ect-61169ea5:#f97316;--ect-63cc1385:#3f3f46;--ect-879b7ebc:#2c2c31;--ect-b9f8de6d:#ae500f;--ect-f59ba8df:#71717a}}:is(html.quarto-light, body.quarto-light, html[data-bs-theme=\"light\"], [data-jp-theme-light=\"true\"], body.vscode-light, body.vscode-high-contrast-light, html[theme=\"light\"]) .ec-theme{--ect-3239c383:#fafafa;--ect-e5dfd507:#94a3b8;--ect-8a2de1d4:#374151;--ect-57425a7e:rgba(15,23,42,0.88);--ect-21ade003:#f1f5f9;--ect-61169ea5:#c2410c;--ect-63cc1385:#d4d4d8;--ect-879b7ebc:#949497;--ect-b9f8de6d:#872d08;--ect-f59ba8df:#a1a1aa}:is(html.quarto-dark, body.quarto-dark, html[data-bs-theme=\"dark\"], [data-jp-theme-light=\"false\"], body.vscode-dark, body.vscode-high-contrast:not(.vscode-high-contrast-light), html[theme=\"dark\"]) .ec-theme{--ect-3239c383:#0d1117;--ect-e5dfd507:#4b5563;--ect-8a2de1d4:#d1d5db;--ect-57425a7e:rgba(241,245,249,0.92);--ect-21ade003:#0f172a;--ect-61169ea5:#f97316;--ect-63cc1385:#3f3f46;--ect-879b7ebc:#2c2c31;--ect-b9f8de6d:#ae500f;--ect-f59ba8df:#71717a}</style><div class=\"ec-plot\" style=\"position:relative;width:fit-content;max-width:100%;margin:1